@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1738 = private unnamed_addr constant [776 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for strings that resemble SQL statements involved in some form\0Astring building operation.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASQL injection is a common attack vector for web applications. Directly\0Ainterpolating user input into SQL statements should always be avoided.\0AInstead, favor parameterized queries, in which the SQL statement is\0Aprovided separately from its parameters, as supported by `psycopg3`\0Aand other database drivers and ORMs.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aquery = \22DELETE FROM foo WHERE id = '%s'\22 % identifier\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [B608: Test for SQL injection](https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/plugins/b608_hardcoded_sql_expressions.html)\0A- [psycopg3: Server-side binding](https://www.psycopg.org/psycopg3/docs/basic/from_pg2.html#server-side-binding)\0A", align 1
