@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1768 = private unnamed_addr constant [474 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary list comprehensions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to use a list comprehension inside a call to `set()`,\0Asince there is an equivalent comprehension for this type.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aset([f(x) for x in foo])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A{f(x) for x in foo}\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may occasionally drop comments\0Awhen rewriting the call. In most cases, though, comments will be preserved.\0A", align 1
